{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyMbg9NvCoQC7VAjsiW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012k9z7E5kw9WsbsdNrfavnh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/xe73303-research/hub/lib/hub && cat retrofit.md && ls -la examples && cat ../README.md | head -80","description":"Read the hub retrofit notes and list examples"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6708,"cache_read_input_tokens":72572,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6708},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944","uuid":"95ca5c90-8f3d-4d8d-a21e-af46d010f660","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:15.521Z","request_id":"req_011CggyMbTknHmYW1ajffZSv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012k9z7E5kw9WsbsdNrfavnh":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/xe73303-research/hub/lib/hub && cat retrofit.md && ls -la examples && cat ../README.md | head -80","description":"Read the hub retrofit notes and list examples"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012k9z7E5kw9WsbsdNrfavnh","type":"tool_result","content":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\ntotal 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:52 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33330 Nov  3 17:52 arena.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 29231 Nov  3 17:52 ghost.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33011 Nov  3 17:52 parallel.html\n# lib/ — the shared 3D stack\n\nLoaded by games using the shared kit from the site root (`/lib/...`), so one\nupgrade here moves those games together. They reach it through the import map in their `<head>`\n(see `kit/README.md`).\n\n| Folder | What | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `three/` | three.js r186 (0.186.1): `three.core.js`, `three.webgpu.js`, `three.tsl.js`, minified; `addons/` = `examples/jsm/` unminified, minus WebGL-only and tooling folders | npm `three@0.186.1` |\n| `rapier/` | Rapier 0.20.0: `rapier-simd.mjs` (from `@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat`) and `rapier.mjs` (from `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat`), wasm inlined | npm |\n| `kit/` | our foundation: boot, renderer, settings and quality tiers, input and touch controls, physics loader, post-processing, sized points, the settings panel | this repo |\n| `vendor/` | immutable versioned package shelf: Three.js 0.180.0–0.186.1 and all 12 official Rapier variants at 0.19.3, 0.20.0 and 0.21.0 | npm, with integrity-checked downloads; see `vendor/README.md` |\n\nThe versioned shelf supports importing older games without migrating their\nrenderer or physics. `pnpm ingest` localizes recognized engine URLs and bare\nimports; copying a game manually still requires its own correct import map.\nThe shared `three/`, `rapier/` and `kit/` paths remain independent of the shelf.\n\n## Upgrading three.js\n\n```bash\nnpm pack three@<version> && tar xzf three-<version>.tgz\nfor f in three.core.js three.webgpu.js three.tsl.js; do\n  npx esbuild package/build/$f --minify --format=esm --target=es2022 --legal-comments=inline --outfile=lib/three/$f\ndone\nrsync -a --delete --exclude-from=lib/three-addons.exclude package/examples/jsm/ lib/three/addons/\n```\n\nThen run `python3 scripts/check3d.py lib/kit/example.html` and a sample of\ngames on both backends, read the three.js migration notes for the revisions\nyou skipped, and update `kit/README.md` if an API moved.\n\n### Local patches\n\n`rsync --delete` above overwrites these; re-apply each one unless the new\nrelease fixes the problem upstream (check with the pipeline count in\n`window.__kit.pipelines`):\n\n- `addons/csm/CSMShadowNode.js`: `_setupFade()` and `_setupStandard()` build\n  their `cameraNear`, `cascades` and `shadowFar` nodes once (`??=` on the\n  instance) instead of on every setup. Otherwise each material build gets a\n  differently named uniform buffer, and every InstancedMesh under cascaded\n  shadows compiles its own shader (Verdant Frontier: 119 pipelines → 27).\n- `three.webgpu.js`, `ViewportTextureNode.getTextureForReference()`: each\n  per-render-target clone of the framebuffer texture gets its own `Source`\n  (`r.source=new t.source.constructor({width:0,height:0})`). Clones shared\n  one image, so a new render target of the same size never re-created its\n  copy texture in the target's format, and transmission or viewport\n  textures failed with \"copyFramebufferToTexture: Source and destination\n  formats do not match\" after a quality switch (Golden Hour).\n\n## Upgrading Rapier\n\nCopy `dist/rapier.mjs` from the `-simd-compat` and `-compat` packages of the\nnew version over `rapier/rapier-simd.mjs` and `rapier/rapier.mjs`, bump\n`physicsInfo.version` in `kit/physics.js`, and re-tune any game whose feel\ndepends on changed defaults.\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944","uuid":"97b1b749-0673-437b-aa92-6d4e34bb47b9","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:15.554Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\ntotal 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:52 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:52 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33330 Nov  3 17:52 arena.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 29231 Nov  3 17:52 ghost.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33011 Nov  3 17:52 parallel.html\n# lib/ — the shared 3D stack\n\nLoaded by games using the shared kit from the site root (`/lib/...`), so one\nupgrade here moves those games together. They reach it through the import map in their `<head>`\n(see `kit/README.md`).\n\n| Folder | What | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| `three/` | three.js r186 (0.186.1): `three.core.js`, `three.webgpu.js`, `three.tsl.js`, minified; `addons/` = `examples/jsm/` unminified, minus WebGL-only and tooling folders | npm `three@0.186.1` |\n| `rapier/` | Rapier 0.20.0: `rapier-simd.mjs` (from `@dimforge/rapier3d-simd-compat`) and `rapier.mjs` (from `@dimforge/rapier3d-compat`), wasm inlined | npm |\n| `kit/` | our foundation: boot, renderer, settings and quality tiers, input and touch controls, physics loader, post-processing, sized points, the settings panel | this repo |\n| `vendor/` | immutable versioned package shelf: Three.js 0.180.0–0.186.1 and all 12 official Rapier variants at 0.19.3, 0.20.0 and 0.21.0 | npm, with integrity-checked downloads; see `vendor/README.md` |\n\nThe versioned shelf supports importing older games without migrating their\nrenderer or physics. `pnpm ingest` localizes recognized engine URLs and bare\nimports; copying a game manually still requires its own correct import map.\nThe shared `three/`, `rapier/` and `kit/` paths remain independent of the shelf.\n\n## Upgrading three.js\n\n```bash\nnpm pack three@<version> && tar xzf three-<version>.tgz\nfor f in three.core.js three.webgpu.js three.tsl.js; do\n  npx esbuild package/build/$f --minify --format=esm --target=es2022 --legal-comments=inline --outfile=lib/three/$f\ndone\nrsync -a --delete --exclude-from=lib/three-addons.exclude package/examples/jsm/ lib/three/addons/\n```\n\nThen run `python3 scripts/check3d.py lib/kit/example.html` and a sample of\ngames on both backends, read the three.js migration notes for the revisions\nyou skipped, and update `kit/README.md` if an API moved.\n\n### Local patches\n\n`rsync --delete` above overwrites these; re-apply each one unless the new\nrelease fixes the problem upstream (check with the pipeline count in\n`window.__kit.pipelines`):\n\n- `addons/csm/CSMShadowNode.js`: `_setupFade()` and `_setupStandard()` build\n  their `cameraNear`, `cascades` and `shadowFar` nodes once (`??=` on the\n  instance) instead of on every setup. Otherwise each material build gets a\n  differently named uniform buffer, and every InstancedMesh under cascaded\n  shadows compiles its own shader (Verdant Frontier: 119 pipelines → 27).\n- `three.webgpu.js`, `ViewportTextureNode.getTextureForReference()`: each\n  per-render-target clone of the framebuffer texture gets its own `Source`\n  (`r.source=new t.source.constructor({width:0,height:0})`). Clones shared\n  one image, so a new render target of the same size never re-created its\n  copy texture in the target's format, and transmission or viewport\n  textures failed with \"copyFramebufferToTexture: Source and destination\n  formats do not match\" after a quality switch (Golden Hour).\n\n## Upgrading Rapier\n\nCopy `dist/rapier.mjs` from the `-simd-compat` and `-compat` packages of the\nnew version over `rapier/rapier-simd.mjs` and `rapier/rapier.mjs`, bump\n`physicsInfo.version` in `kit/physics.js`, and re-tune any game whose feel\ndepends on changed defaults.","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012k9z7E5kw9WsbsdNrfavnh","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
