{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggySEWp1hUk7ywHeeGiS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018ugnSVTYTsLsNUVA5wGbL3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/xe73303-research/engine/dist/handoff && sed -n 402,606p AI_GUIDE.md | grep -n -i -A12 \"^### Sports\\|^- \\*\\*Sports\\|sports (\\|^### .*attract\\|attract\" | head -80","description":"Find the sports recipe and attract mode notes in the guide"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11949,"cache_read_input_tokens":142037,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11949},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944","uuid":"4a09d49e-752f-4068-ab20-5dea71d9dedb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:53:10.351Z","request_id":"req_011CggySEJAGtq5fRiKfDBir","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018ugnSVTYTsLsNUVA5wGbL3":{"command":"cd /home/micha/.cache/xe73303-research/engine/dist/handoff && sed -n 402,606p AI_GUIDE.md | grep -n -i -A12 \"^### Sports\\|^- \\*\\*Sports\\|sports (\\|^### .*attract\\|attract\" | head -80","description":"Find the sports recipe and attract mode notes in the guide"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018ugnSVTYTsLsNUVA5wGbL3","type":"tool_result","content":"51:- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\n52-- A maze is an `E.Grid` with `E.GridMover`s: the player's turn asked early is kept (`{ keep: true }`); a chaser picks, at each cell, the open way nearest its own target (never straight back). Moths fly in on `E.Path`s and turn with `r.sprite`'s `rot`; rocks drift with `E.wrap` and draw at every edge they cross.\n53-- Each game's demo is its own bot, playing the real rules; a remaster (light, rigs, glow) with the classic look one key and one setting away.\n54-\n55-**Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero).** Start from the KART slice (the mode7 and drive modules).\n56-- The track is a TileMap: its walls bounce the karts, its floor tags (`grass`, `sand`, `boost`, ...) slow or boost them (`E.Car`'s `surfaces`), and `E.Mode7({ floor: (x, y) => [r, g, b] })` draws it from the same cells. The racing line is a closed `E.Path` through the track's middle: `E.Race({ path, laps: 3 })` counts laps through its checkpoints in order (a shortcut counts nothing), gives places, and drives every car not a player's (`race.add(car, { input })` for a player, `{ ai: { skill } }` for the rest).\n57-- Each step `race.update(dt, map)` (it moves every car), then the camera behind yours, turning after it more slowly than the kart turns (a drift shows): `m7.cam = cam; m7.chase({ x, y, angle: camAngle }, { back: 42, h: 24 })`. Draw the karts with `m7.add(x, y, z, (g, sx, sy, k) => ...)`: a few boxes through `m7.view(k)`'s projection and the rig seated (`down: .4`) in the middle, sorted far to near from the camera's side.\n58-- Two players: `game.allowJoin({ max: 2 })`, `game.splitScreen(2, { layout: 'rows' })`, and in `draw` each viewport its own camera: `m7.draw(r, cams[r.viewport.i])`, `race.hud(r, players[r.viewport.i])`. On a phone the gas goes on by itself (`car.o.auto`), the stick steers, DRIFT and ITEM are buttons; held upright, draw from further back with a wider field of view.\n59-\n60-**Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Hang-On).** Start from the ROAD slice (the road module).\n61-- `E.Road` is the course: `road.add(n, { curve, hill, tunnel, colors })` stretch by stretch; scenery with `road.place(z, offset, sprite, scale)` (`E.prop('palm').frames[0]` works), traffic as `cars: [{ z, x, w, draw }]` passed to `road.draw`. The player is a position (`z` along, `x` across in half roads) and a speed, not a body.\n62-- Each step: `x -= road.curveAt(z) * speed² * k` throws the car outward on a bend (make the hardest faster than the player can steer: they slow down), off the road (`|x| > 1`) it slows, `road.hits(z, x, w)` crashes it into the scenery (put it back on the road), and a car close in `z` and `x` bumps it. A clock that counts down and checkpoints that add time make the race.\n63-\n--\n167:**Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).** Start from the SPORTS slice: two against two in a walled cage, up to four players.\n168-- The field is a `TileMap` cage in `threequarter` (boards that cut low before the camera, nets); the ball and the players are `E.Body`s. The ball bounces off the ground and the boards (`bounce`), and curls: turn its velocity a little across its path each step while the shooter pushes sideways (aftertouch).\n169-- A pass leads the teammate (aim where it is going, not where it is); a lob over a defender is `E.arc(from, to, gravity, { apex })`, the throw that lands at its feet; a shot's power fills a meter while its button is held and goes on letting go.\n170-- The players a person doesn't run play by formation, by where the ball is: with it, the other one runs ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` lets players 2 to 4 in, each taking a side's next player.\n171-\n172-**First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder).** The 3D CRAWLER kit (the grid module). The 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes over a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell; each step and quarter turn is a tween, so the view glides. Gates are `world.thing('door')`s that rise (`world.unlock` for one with a key); the monsters walk an `E.Grid` cell to cell; `E.Fog` keeps what the party has seen for the automap; `E.Turns` in `'atb'` is real time (Dungeon Master), in `'speed'` the dungeon waits for the party (Wizardry). The party's portraits sit under the view (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n173-\n174-**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n175-- One fixed room in `topdown` (`res: [320, 240]`, `expand`): the hero a `Body` moved by `input.move()`, the left stick or WASD; it fires the way the right stick points (`input.padAim`), else toward the mouse (`input.pointer()` to a ground point), else the way it moves, a shot every 0.08 s from an `E.Bullets` pool (`plane: 'ground'`).\n176-- Waves spawn from the room's edges by a timeline; grunts walk straight at the hero, others wander, hulks can't be killed, humans to rescue for points. `cam.shake` and `game.freeze(.03)` on every kill keep it loud; `E.Arcade` keeps the score, the lives and the table.\n177-\n178-**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n179-- The arena is an `E.Grid` of hard blocks on even cells and soft blocks to break; players and foes are `E.GridMover`s (a turn asked early is kept).\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944","uuid":"ae9a8b23-a57d-4a25-b58d-96fbd6a82bdc","timesta