wport.i])`, `race.hud(r, players[r.viewport.i])`. On a phone the gas goes on by itself (`car.o.auto`), the stick steers, DRIFT and ITEM are buttons; held upright, draw from further back with a wider field of view.\n59-\n60-**Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Hang-On).** Start from the ROAD slice (the road module).\n61-- `E.Road` is the course: `road.add(n, { curve, hill, tunnel, colors })` stretch by stretch; scenery with `road.place(z, offset, sprite, scale)` (`E.prop('palm').frames[0]` works), traffic as `cars: [{ z, x, w, draw }]` passed to `road.draw`. The player is a position (`z` along, `x` across in half roads) and a speed, not a body.\n62-- Each step: `x -= road.curveAt(z) * speed² * k` throws the car outward on a bend (make the hardest faster than the player can steer: they slow down), off the road (`|x| > 1`) it slows, `road.hits(z, x, w)` crashes it into the scenery (put it back on the road), and a car close in `z` and `x` bumps it. A clock that counts down and checkpoints that add time make the race.\n63-\n--\n167:**Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).** Start from the SPORTS slice: two against two in a walled cage, up to four players.\n168-- The field is a `TileMap` cage in `threequarter` (boards that cut low before the camera, nets); the ball and the players are `E.Body`s. The ball bounces off the ground and the boards (`bounce`), and curls: turn its velocity a little across its path each step while the shooter pushes sideways (aftertouch).\n169-- A pass leads the teammate (aim where it is going, not where it is); a lob over a defender is `E.arc(from, to, gravity, { apex })`, the throw that lands at its feet; a shot's power fills a meter while its button is held and goes on letting go.\n170-- The players a person doesn't run play by formation, by where the ball is: with it, the other one runs ahead on the far side; without it, the nearer presses and the other covers the goal. `game.allowJoin({ max: 4 })` lets players 2 to 4 in, each taking a side's next player.\n171-\n172-**First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder).** The 3D CRAWLER kit (the grid module). The 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the party's eyes over a level of 2 x 2 tiles a cell; each step and quarter turn is a tween, so the view glides. Gates are `world.thing('door')`s that rise (`world.unlock` for one with a key); the monsters walk an `E.Grid` cell to cell; `E.Fog` keeps what the party has seen for the automap; `E.Turns` in `'atb'` is real time (Dungeon Master), in `'speed'` the dungeon waits for the party (Wizardry). The party's portraits sit under the view (`rig.drawPortrait`).\n173-\n174-**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n175-- One fixed room in `topdown` (`res: [320, 240]`, `expand`): the hero a `Body` moved by `input.move()`, the left stick or WASD; it fires the way the right stick points (`input.padAim`), else toward the mouse (`input.pointer()` to a ground point), else the way it moves, a shot every 0.08 s from an `E.Bullets` pool (`plane: 'ground'`).\n176-- Waves spawn from the room's edges by a timeline; grunts walk straight at the hero, others wander, hulks can't be killed, humans to rescue for points. `cam.shake` and `game.freeze(.03)` on every kill keep it loud; `E.Arcade` keeps the score, the lives and the table.\n177-\n178-**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n179-- The arena is an `E.Grid` of hard blocks on even cells and soft blocks to break; players and foes are `E.GridMover`s (a turn asked early is kept).","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018ugnSVTYTsLsNUVA5wGbL3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
