551,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":189481,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":6551},\"output_tokens\":5,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8\",\"uuid\":\"990aaf73-5472-43da-bca1-65b8935cca97\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:57:19.206Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011Cggyk5Uawj3H4AWMgU94h\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01Eq7RLRAHmKnLNDo2LYJmdx\":{\"query\":\"Time Crisis 3 arcade 2002 Nex Entertainment Namco weapon select system pedal PS2 2003\",\"mode\":\"standard\"}}}"," {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01Eq7RLRAHmKnLNDo2LYJmdx\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"Web search results for query: \\\"Time Crisis 3 arcade 2002 Nex Entertainment Namco weapon select system pedal PS2 2003\\\"\\n\\nLinks: [{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Crisis_3\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukano\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://wikiwand.com/en/articles/Time_Crisis_3\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.gamingnexus.com/Article/360/Time-Crisis-3\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"cloud.clz.com\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cloud.clz.com/howema/games/detail/514270\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Highway Games visit arcoodapinball.com\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.highwaygames.com/arcade-machines/time-crisis-3-dx-arcade-machine-8797/\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Developer |\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://timecrisispedia.fandom.com/wiki/File:21006001.jpg\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Archives by Day\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://worthplaying.com/article/2003/10/13/previews/13092\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3 - PS2\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://cdn0.spong.com/game/11034495\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3 PS2\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://gamepressure.com/games/time-crisis-3/zd1dd4\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/3985/\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"time crisis 3 playstation 2\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://ava.ead.domalberto.edu.br/time-crisis-3-playstation-2\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"www.arcade-history.com\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/2903/?o=2\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Time_Crisis_3\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Time_Crisis\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://mobileapps.wikiwand.com/en/Time_Crisis_3\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"emporiumarcadebar.com\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://emporiumarcadebar.com/?p=14207\\\"},{\\\"title\\\":\\\"Time Crisis 3 (PlayStation 2 [NA])\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://gameventory.app/playstation-2-na/time-crisis-3\\\"}]\\n\\nThe search results support most of your query, with one caveat on dates.\\n\\n- **Dates:** Sources disagree on the arcade release year. One says it came out in 2002 in Japan and 2003 in North America, while another notes the title screen shows 2002 as the development year and the game was shown at the 2003 AOU show before its April 1, 2003 Japanese release. The PS2 version came out in October 2003 in North America and Europe, and in November 2003 in Japan.\\n- **Developer and publisher:** Namco published the game, and Nextech is credited as co-developer. One category page also lists Nex Entertainment, which fits your query's mention of that company, but I found no source that spells out its exact role.\\n- **Weapon select:** This is the main new feature. One review says the series' first weapon-switching system set it apart from earlier entries, which gave players only specific weapons at fixed points. The PS2 version offers four weapons: machine gun, handgun, shotgun, and grenade.\\n- **Pedal:** The arcade version keeps the foot pedal for ducking and advancing. On PS2, a button on the GunCon 2 gun replaces it.\\n- **Other PS2 details:** The PS2 version supports the GunCon 2 and two-player play, including linking two PS2s and two TVs.\\n\\n\\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"bbb0a1ea-12f9-46f9-9677-d2d253a967c8\",\"uuid\":\"b6abc503-b17e-435e-b7db-24212f2bd731\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:57:25.391Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"query\":\"Time Crisis 3 arcade 2002 Nex Entertainment Namco weapon select system pedal PS2 2003\",\"results\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"srvtoolu_0172YraKFiJTfvt2dDoFXNGE\",\"content\":[{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Time_Crisis_3\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://Www.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lukano\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://wikiwand.com/en/articles/Time_Crisis_3\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://www.gamingnexus.com/Article/360/Time-Crisis-3\"},{\"title\":\"cloud.clz.com\",\"url\":\"https://cloud.clz.com/howema/games/detail/514270\"},{\"title\":\"Highway Games visit arcoodapinball.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.highwaygames.com/arcade-machines/time-crisis-3-dx-arcade-machine-8797/\"},{\"title\":\"Developer |\",\"url\":\"https://timecrisispedia.fandom.com/wiki/File:21006001.jpg\"},{\"title\":\"Archives by Day\",\"url\":\"https://worthplaying.com/article/2003/10/13/previews/13092\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3 - PS2\",\"url\":\"https://cdn0.spong.com/game/11034495\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3 PS2\",\"url\":\"https://gamepressure.com/games/time-crisis-3/zd1dd4\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/3985/\"},{\"title\":\"time crisis 3 playstation 2\",\"url\":\"https://ava.ead.domalberto.edu.br/time-crisis-3-playstation-2\"},{\"title\":\"www.arcade-history.com\",\"url\":\"https://www.arcade-history.com/game/2903/?o=2\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://strategywiki.org/wiki/Time_Crisis_3\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis\",\"url\":\"https://giantbomb.com/wiki/Games/Time_Crisis\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3\",\"url\":\"https://mobileapps.wikiwand.com/en/Time_Crisis_3\"},{\"title\":\"emporiumarcadebar.com\",\"url\":\"https://emporiumarcadebar.com/?p=14207\"},{\"title\":\"Time Crisis 3 (PlayStation 2 [NA])\",\"url\":\"https://gameventory.app/playstation-2-na/time-crisis-3\"}]},\"The search results support most of your query, with one caveat on dates.\\n\\n- **Dates:** Sources disagree on the arcade release year. One says it came out in 2002 in Japan and 2003 in North America, while another notes the title screen shows 2002 as the development year and the game was shown at the 2003 AOU show before its April 1, 2003 Japanese release. The PS2 version came out in October 2003 in North America and Europe, and in November 2003 in Japan.\\n- **Developer and publisher:** Namco published the game, and Nextech is credited as co-developer. One category page also lists Nex Entertainment, which fits your query's mention of that company, but I found no source that spells out its exact role.\\n- **Weapon select:** This is the main new feature. One review says the series' first weapon-switching system set it apart from earlier entries, which gave players only specific weapons at fixed points. The PS2 version offers four weapons: machine gun, handgun, shotgun, and grenade.\\n- **Pedal:** The arcade version keeps the foot pedal for ducking and advancing. On PS2, a button on the GunCon 2 gun replaces it.\\n- **Other PS2 details:** The PS2 version supports the GunCon 2 and two-player play, including linking two PS2s and two TVs.\"],\"durationSeconds\":6.180467359000002,\"searchCount\":1},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01Eq7RLRAHmKnLNDo2LYJmdx\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"re