{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01R6GM8ED2Ydwr2bf4jp5yRq","type":"tool_result","content":"  1470  20957 PLAN.md\n# Ice Hoc-Kaboom\n\n**The build plan for the game TASK.md describes** (source: ice hockey, over-the-top arcade style). Read TASK.md first, then\n9:## 0. The game at a glance\n46:### Title pick (as TASK.md says)\n54:## 1. Deliverables, folders and working rules\n98:## 2. Engine and hub facts the build relies on (verified while planning)\n164:## 3. Design decisions in brief (why this shape)\n177:## 4. Engine changes (make them in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, log each in ENGINE-CHANGES.md)\n209:## 5. Architecture\n211:### 5.1 Runtime shape\n228:### 5.2 Source modules (`src/`, concatenated in this order into one IIFE)\n268:### 5.3 Entities (plain objects, owned by `Match`)\n281:### 5.4 The match step (fixed order; deterministic; `Match.step(dt)`)\n303:### 5.5 Debug handle (tests and tools read it)\n312:## 6. Controls (one game on every device)\n314:### 6.1 Actions and default bindings (`HOCKEY_KEYS`, built from `E.Input.DEFAULT`'s menu keys)\n345:### 6.2 Prompts and glyphs\n358:## 7. Systems (rules, numbers, behavior)\n362:### 7.1 The rink (`Rink`)\n396:### 7.2 Skating (`Skater.skateStep`, pure: the network prediction runs it too)\n416:### 7.3 The puck (`Puck`)\n437:### 7.4 Passing\n454:### 7.5 Shooting\n469:### 7.6 Goalies (`Goalie`)\n493:### 7.7 Checking, the glass, grudges (`Hits`)\n511:### 7.8 Deke and poke\n519:### 7.9 Chirping (`chirp`)\n525:### 7.10 The BOOM meter and KABOOM mode (`Boom`)\n541:### 7.11 Fights and the sin bin (`Fight`)\n568:### 7.12 Fan throws, power-ups and hazards (`Items`)\n604:### 7.13 Team AI (`AI`)\n630:### 7.14 Match flow (`Match`)\n666:### 7.15 Camera director (`Cam`)\n676:### 7.16 Instant replay (`Replay`)\n687:### 7.17 Commentary (`Talk`)\n699:### 7.18 HUD (`Hud`; it keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a 92% title-safe area)\n718:## 8. Art direction\n753:## 9. Animation (the engine's procedural rigs plus new hockey motion)\n791:## 10. Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n793:### 10.1 Voices: babble (Animalese/Simlish style)\n808:### 10.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices; custom graphs where noted)\n821:### 10.3 Crowd and organ\n832:### 10.4 Music (engine song format; the new `organ` and `brass` waves; named layers)\n853:## 11. Content\n855:### 11.1 Teams (3 skaters + 1 goalie each; ratings 1–5: Spd / Sht / Pas / Hit / Fgt / Hnd; goalies Rfx / Size / Reb)\n878:### 11.2 Arenas\n892:### 11.3 Story: THE CUP RUN\n979:### 11.4 Practice: Coach Marge's Drills (at the Ol' Icebox, house lights half on)\n994:### 11.5 Text pools (in `07-data-text.js`; sizes are the minimums)\n1000:## 12. Screens and flows (10-foot UI)\n1036:### 12.1 About / Credits screen\n1046:## 13. Settings (via `menu.settings`; the engine's Display, Sound, Comfort and Controls stay)\n1054:## 14. Online: AI Hub sessions (`Net`, shared-world)\n1056:### 14.1 Page tags (in `<head>`, after the session client)\n1068:### 14.2 Flow (when `AIHub.active`)\n1102:### 14.3 Netcode (it stays within 20 messages a second per copy and 16 KB per message)\n1125:## 15. Attract mode, touch-only devices and dev mode\n1127:### 15.1 Attract mode (scene `attract`)\n1148:### 15.2 Touch-only devices\n1157:### 15.3 Dev mode (scene overlay `Dev`, from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item; also `#dev`)\n1180:## 16. Build order and milestones\n1199:## 17. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1215:## 18. Testing\n1224:### 18.1 Unit (pure functions)\n1232:### 18.2 Systems (headless game)\n1249:### 18.3 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (`tests/play-story.mjs`)\n1264:### 18.4 Other headless suites\n1274:### 18.5 Fake-hub network test (headless, Node)\n1281:### 18.6 Browser suites (Playwright 1.63, Chromium; `TMPDIR` set)\n1295:### 18.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge; `tests/shots.mjs`)\n1304:## 19. Definition of done (TASK.md → where it is met)\n1331:## Appendix A: Tuning defaults (`T`; every row is a Dev slider)\n1377:## Appendix B: Event catalogue (`Bus`; consumers: stats, objectives, Talk, Fx, Crowd, Net, Replay)\n1389:## Appendix C: Cutscene data format\n1406:## Appendix D: Writing samples (the voice to match; TEXT holds the full pools)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944","uuid":"1de811d2-1651-42a9-8e1b-b7673befd109","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:25:49.057Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  1470  20957 PLAN.md\n# Ice Hoc-Kaboom\n\n**The build plan for the game TASK.md describes** (source: ice hockey, over-the-top arcade style). Read TASK.md first, then\n9:## 0. The game at a glance\n46:### Title pick (as TASK.md says)\n54:## 1. Deliverables, folders and working rules\n98:## 2. Engine and hub facts the build relies on (verified while planning)\n164:## 3. Design decisions in brief (why this shape)\n177:## 4. Engine changes (make them in `engine/my-3d2dge.js`, log each in ENGINE-CHANGES.md)\n209:## 5. Architecture\n211:### 5.1 Runtime shape\n228:### 5.2 Source modules (`src/`, concatenated in this order into one IIFE)\n268:### 5.3 Entities (plain objects, owned by `Match`)\n281:### 5.4 The match step (fixed order; deterministic; `Match.step(dt)`)\n303:### 5.5 Debug handle (tests and tools read it)\n312:## 6. Controls (one game on every device)\n314:### 6.1 Actions and default bindings (`HOCKEY_KEYS`, built from `E.Input.DEFAULT`'s menu keys)\n345:### 6.2 Prompts and glyphs\n358:## 7. Systems (rules, numbers, behavior)\n362:### 7.1 The rink (`Rink`)\n396:### 7.2 Skating (`Skater.skateStep`, pure: the network prediction runs it too)\n416:### 7.3 The puck (`Puck`)\n437:### 7.4 Passing\n454:### 7.5 Shooting\n469:### 7.6 Goalies (`Goalie`)\n493:### 7.7 Checking, the glass, grudges (`Hits`)\n511:### 7.8 Deke and poke\n519:### 7.9 Chirping (`chirp`)\n525:### 7.10 The BOOM meter and KABOOM mode (`Boom`)\n541:### 7.11 Fights and the sin bin (`Fight`)\n568:### 7.12 Fan throws, power-ups and hazards (`Items`)\n604:### 7.13 Team AI (`AI`)\n630:### 7.14 Match flow (`Match`)\n666:### 7.15 Camera director (`Cam`)\n676:### 7.16 Instant replay (`Replay`)\n687:### 7.17 Commentary (`Talk`)\n699:### 7.18 HUD (`Hud`; it keeps clear of `game.cornerArea()` and inside a 92% title-safe area)\n718:## 8. Art direction\n753:## 9. Animation (the engine's procedural rigs plus new hockey motion)\n791:## 10. Audio (all synthesized in code; no audio files)\n793:### 10.1 Voices: babble (Animalese/Simlish style)\n808:### 10.2 Sound effects (`audio.define` voices; custom graphs where noted)\n821:### 10.3 Crowd and organ\n832:### 10.4 Music (engine song format; the new `organ` and `brass` waves; named layers)\n853:## 11. Content\n855:### 11.1 Teams (3 skaters + 1 goalie each; ratings 1–5: Spd / Sht / Pas / Hit / Fgt / Hnd; goalies Rfx / Size / Reb)\n878:### 11.2 Arenas\n892:### 11.3 Story: THE CUP RUN\n979:### 11.4 Practice: Coach Marge's Drills (at the Ol' Icebox, house lights half on)\n994:### 11.5 Text pools (in `07-data-text.js`; sizes are the minimums)\n1000:## 12. Screens and flows (10-foot UI)\n1036:### 12.1 About / Credits screen\n1046:## 13. Settings (via `menu.settings`; the engine's Display, Sound, Comfort and Controls stay)\n1054:## 14. Online: AI Hub sessions (`Net`, shared-world)\n1056:### 14.1 Page tags (in `<head>`, after the session client)\n1068:### 14.2 Flow (when `AIHub.active`)\n1102:### 14.3 Netcode (it stays within 20 messages a second per copy and 16 KB per message)\n1125:## 15. Attract mode, touch-only devices and dev mode\n1127:### 15.1 Attract mode (scene `attract`)\n1148:### 15.2 Touch-only devices\n1157:### 15.3 Dev mode (scene overlay `Dev`, from the pause menu's **Dev Mode** item; also `#dev`)\n1180:## 16. Build order and milestones\n1199:## 17. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1215:## 18. Testing\n1224:### 18.1 Unit (pure functions)\n1232:### 18.2 Systems (headless game)\n1249:### 18.3 Scripted playthrough of the whole game (`tests/play-story.mjs`)\n1264:### 18.4 Other headless suites\n1274:### 18.5 Fake-hub network test (headless, Node)\n1281:### 18.6 Browser suites (Playwright 1.63, Chromium; `TMPDIR` set)\n1295:### 18.7 Screenshots (only for what scripts can't judge; `tests/shots.mjs`)\n1304:## 19. Definition of done (TASK.md → where it is met)\n1331:## Appendix A: Tuning defaults (`T`; every row is a Dev slider)\n1377:## Appendix B: Event catalogue (`Bus`; consumers: stats, objectives, Talk, Fx, Crowd, Net, Replay)\n1389:## Appendix C: Cutscene data format\n1406:## Appendix D: Writing samples (the voice to match; TEXT holds the full pools)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01R6GM8ED2Ydwr2bf4jp5yRq","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
