{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NjFXtGyyTftKSda4CkG6pP","type":"tool_result","content":"209\t## 5. Architecture\n210\t\n211\t### 5.1 Runtime shape\n212\t- **One `E.Game`**: `new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'threequarter',\n213\t  input: HOCKEY_KEYS, menu: { items: [['Dev Mode', () => Dev.open()]], settings: SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES,\n214\t  quit: 'title' }, autoPause: !hub, id: 'ice-hoc-kaboom' })`. In an AI Hub session, build it with `quit: false`, no\n215\t  Dev Mode item and `autoPause: false` (section 14).\n216\t- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title: 'ICE HOC-KABOOM', steps } })`):\n217\t  `title`, `attract`, `sides` (exhibition side select), `setup` (exhibition teams, arena, options), `storymap`,\n218\t  `cutscene`, `match` (pausable: all hockey play, including the shootout and the story games), `flood` (pausable: the\n219\t  intermission minigame), `results`, `practice` (pausable: drills), `records`, `about`, `credits`, `session` (AI Hub:\n220\t  card → play → end) and `lab` (dev only: the animation lab).\n221\t- **Boot steps**: bake the floor TileMap of the first arena (the others lazily at match start, behind the boot or\n222\t  a \"loading\" card); register the synth voices and songs; build the logo sprites; validate the data tables (fail loudly\n223\t  in dev); load the save.\n224\t- **Deep links** (not in sessions; for tests and tools): `#attract`, `#story/<1-5>`, `#cutscene/<id>`,\n225\t  `#match/<home>/<away>/<arena>`, `#fight`, `#kaboom`, `#shootout`, `#flood`, `#practice/<1-7>`, `#results`,\n226\t  `#about`, `#records`, `#lab`, `#dev` (a match with the Dev panel open).\n227\t\n228\t### 5.2 Source modules (`src/`, concatenated in this order into one IIFE)\n229\tEach module is `const Name = (() => { … return { … }; })();`, the kit's style. Simulation modules never touch the\n230\tDOM, audio or particles directly: they emit events (5.4).\n231\t\n232\t| File | Module | Responsibility |\n233\t|---|---|---|\n234\t| `00-head.js` | – | `'use strict'`, `const E = My3D2dge`, the hub flags (`HUB = window.AIHub && AIHub.active`), the `game` instance, short-hands |\n235\t| `01-util.js` | `U` | math (angle helpers, segment–circle and segment–segment tests, quantize), RNG streams `RNG.sim` / `RNG.fx` (from `E.rng`), name sanitizer (NFD → ASCII; other characters → `?`) |\n236\t| `02-events.js` | `Bus` | `emit(type, data)`, `on(type, fn)`; a per-match event log |\n237\t| `03-tuning.js` | `T` | every tunable number: defaults, live values, slider metadata (`min`, `max`, `step`, `group`, `label`), `reset(key)`, `resetAll()`, persisted in `E.store('dev:tuning')` |\n238\t| `04-data-teams.js` | `TEAMS` | 6 teams (section 11.1): colors, logos (string sprites), players, ratings, voices, goal songs |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a68f2607-3679-4041-bc34-a15f5427a944","uuid":"56a62aa0-084b-4e34-951c-3caefce8d5b6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:26:03.883Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174816__xe73303/work/PLAN.md","content":"## 5. Architecture\n\n### 5.1 Runtime shape\n- **One `E.Game`**: `new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'threequarter',\n  input: HOCKEY_KEYS, menu: { items: [['Dev Mode', () => Dev.open()]], settings: SETTINGS, controls: CONTROL_NAMES,\n  quit: 'title' }, autoPause: !hub, id: 'ice-hoc-kaboom' })`. In an AI Hub session, build it with `quit: false`, no\n  Dev Mode item and `autoPause: false` (section 14).\n- **Scenes** (`game.start({ scenes, scene, boot: { title: 'ICE HOC-KABOOM', steps } })`):\n  `title`, `attract`, `sides` (exhibition side select), `setup` (exhibition teams, arena, options), `storymap`,\n  `cutscene`, `match` (pausable: all hockey play, including the shootout and the story games), `flood` (pausable: the\n  intermission minigame), `results`, `practice` (pausable: drills), `records`, `about`, `credits`, `session` (AI Hub:\n  card → play → end) and `lab` (dev only: the animation lab).\n- **Boot steps**: bake the floor TileMap of the first arena (the others lazily at match start, behind the boot or\n  a \"loading\" card); register the synth voices and songs; build the logo sprites; validate the data tables (fail loudly\n  in dev); load the save.\n- **Deep links** (not in sessions; for tests and tools): `#attract`, `#story/<1-5>`, `#cutscene/<id>`,\n  `#match/<home>/<away>/<arena>`, `#fight`, `#kaboom`, `#shootout`, `#flood`, `#practice/<1-7>`, `#results`,\n  `#about`, `#records`, `#lab`, `#dev` (a match with the Dev panel open).\n\n### 5.2 Source modules (`src/`, concatenated in this order into one IIFE)\nEach module is `const Name = (() => { … return { … }; })();`, the kit's style. Simulation modules never touch the\nDOM, audio or particles directly: they emit events (5.4).\n\n| File | Module | Responsibility |\n|---|---|---|\n| `00-head.js` | – | `'use strict'`, `const E = My3D2dge`, the hub flags (`HUB = window.AIHub && AIHub.active`), the `game` instance, short-hands |\n| `01-util.js` | `U` | math (angle helpers, segment–circle and segment–segment tests, quantize), RNG streams `RNG.sim` / `RNG.fx` (from `E.rng`), name sanitizer (NFD → ASCII; other characters → `?`) |\n| `02-events.js` | `Bus` | `emit(type, data)`, `on(type, fn)`; a per-match event log |\n| `03-tuning.js` | `T` | every tunable number: defaults, live values, slider metadata (`min`, `max`, `step`, `group`, `label`), `reset(key)`, `resetAll()`, persisted in `E.store('dev:tuning')` |\n| `04-data-teams.js` | `TEAMS` | 6 teams (section 11.1): colors, logos (string sprites), players, ratings, voices, goal songs |","numLines":30,"startLine":209,"totalLines":1471}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NjFXtGyyTftKSda4CkG6pP","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
